## Sess210 findings (arm A mechanism, mostly proven from saved logs)
Chain on test2 (mirrors on other victims):
1. test2 holds EX on hot ino 12585547; pair-peer waits (SESS50-STARVE repeats).
2. noino release fence for it needs whole-AIL drain (mxfs_noino_drain_fence,
   xfs_mxfs_dlm.c:19290). AIL min FROZEN at ino 12585558's INODE item
   lsn=0x30001e1e7 → 8 stalls → P-NOINO-DRAIN-STUCK → RELFENCE-WEDGE →
   shutdown (15:49:10).
3. 12585558 timeline (all 15:48:50): acquire EX + reload → local unlink
   (P82-ADD bucket=16 nlink=0) → peer BAST 3ms later, EX RELEASED
   (P141-UNLK-EXCLR, P70-BP EXIT=full) → THEN inactivation ran (P19-B3DEC
   will_skip=0, dlm_mode=0=NL but dlm_locked=1, b4_noauth=0) → ifree committed
   → dirty item (fields=0x1) at frozen lsn.
4. PROVEN from code: flush_out (xfs_inode.c:8168) consumes ili_fields on EVERY
   xfs_iflush entry incl. P119/P17B/P25 skip paths. Frozen item had fields=0x1
   last=0x0 flushing=0 for 20s ⇒ xfs_iflush NEVER ENTERED. So the repeated skip
   is in xfs_iflush_cluster pre-checks (xfs_inode.c:8851-8913): IRECLAIM/
   IFLUSHING, PINNED (pin=0 → ruled out), or ILOCK_NOWAIT_FAIL.
5. Leading hypothesis (OPEN, needs instrumented repro): thread holds
   ILOCK(12585558) blocked re-acquiring DLM EX from test14 (its rsync pair,
   itself wedging) = documented "ILOCK held across CAW poll" design tension.
   Cross-pair circular wait: test2 holds 12585547 (test14 waits), test14 holds
   12585558 (test2's ILOCK holder waits) → both fences freeze → both die.
   Consistent: victims pair exactly on rsync_paired pairing; test1 later died
   waiting EX on 12585558 (test14 took it, wedged, never released).
6. Instrumentation EXISTS: mxfs_ailstuck_probe knob → P129-CLSKIP names skip
   reason + ILOCK owner (sched_show_task). P129-IPUSH in inode_item_push too.

## Next steps (in order)
1. LEDGER arm A (critical; use mechanism above) + arm B (critical) in
   tests/criteria/OPEN_DEFECTS.json via defects.sh conventions.
2. Fix scripts/module_swap_deploy.sh: pkill -f → pkill -x (known trap).
3. Re-prep rig (mkfs), full board to confirm .474 baseline healthy.
4. Repro arm A: enable mxfs_ailstuck_probe on all nodes, run rsync_paired
   under contention (swap may NOT be required — mechanism is pairing +
   BAST-vs-inactivation race, not the swap itself; sess209 disproved
   stranded-AG/swap theories). RULE 0 budget: lap ≈ 60-90s healthy.
5. On P129-CLSKIP evidence naming the skip: RULE-5 GPT consult on fix design
   (candidates: inactivation must not commit ifree after authority loss —
   b4_noauth hole where dlm_locked=1 masks NL mode; or fence must handle
   ILOCKed-but-DLM-blocked items; or bound fence + requeue vs shutdown).
6. Then resume #18 P95-NL-UNDER-HOLD probe (live in .474) per sess208.

